invariant: INV-26
file: quic_packet.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: a TRANSPORT=quic build takes the AES suite, so a server names
  AES-GCM in its ServerHello while quic_packet.c protects every Handshake
  and 1-RTT packet with ChaCha20-Poly1305. RFC 9001 section 5.3 makes the
  packet AEAD the negotiated one, so no client can read the flight. The
  pair compiles and every unit test passes; quic_packet.c's refusal
  is the only check, and this edit removes it.

--- old
#ifdef CH_SUITE_AES_GCM
#error "CH_SUITE_AES_GCM is refused under CH_TRANSPORT_QUIC: QUIC packets here run ChaCha20 alone"
#endif
--- new
